### Base
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Login as seeded Alice
# @name loginAlice
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!"
}

###
@aliceToken = {{loginAlice.response.body.token}}

### 2) List accounts
GET {{host}}/api/accounts?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 3) List categories
GET {{host}}/api/categories?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 4) List transactions filtered by type/date
GET {{host}}/api/transactions?type=EXPENSE&from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 5) Create valid transaction
# @name createTx
POST {{host}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": 2001,
  "categoryId": 3002,
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "amount": 45.75,
  "description": "Snacks",
  "date": "2026-10-12"
}

###
@txId = {{createTx.response.body.id}}

### 6) Get created transaction
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 7) Insights overview
GET {{host}}/api/insights/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 8) Insights by category
GET {{host}}/api/insights/by-category?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 9) Insights monthly
GET {{host}}/api/insights/monthly
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 10) Validation error (amount must be >= 0.01)
POST {{host}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": 2001,
  "categoryId": 3002,
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "amount": 0.00,
  "description": "Invalid amount",
  "date": "2026-10-12"
}

### 11) Auth error (missing token)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts

### 12) Not found error
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}




### 1) Login with seeded user (expect 200)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!"
}

### 2) Capture token from login response
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 3) Check token exists by calling protected endpoint (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Missing token should fail (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts?page=0&size=5

### 5) Invalid token should fail (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.value

### 6) Wrong password should fail (expect 401)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPass!"
}

### 7) Non-existent user should fail (expect 401)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nouser@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!"
}

### 8) Register new user then login (expect 201 then 200)
# @name registerNew
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Temp User",
  "email": "temp.user.2026@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!"
}

###
# @name loginNew
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "temp.user.2026@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ngPass!"
}

### 9) Use newly issued token on protected endpoint (expect 200)
@newToken = {{loginNew.response.body.token}}
GET {{host}}/api/categories?page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{newToken}}